WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
I won't use modal dialogs when I can get this information later, in another way,

2
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.300
or when it isn't that important in the first place. So why not use a modal dialog here?

3
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:15.940
Instead, I can show the user a message asking if they can give me this data now, and if they say yes,

4
00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:21.600
then they see a modal dialog, or any page, with the data I want to ask for.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.800
Otherwise, I don't need a modal dialog,

6
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:29.300
when I can get this information later, or it isn't important, or it won't help right now

7
00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:32.660
in the flow the user is going through, or in the main steps they're taking.

8
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:38.000
Also, as we said, a modal dialog cuts the user off from the data they're working with

9
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.600
or the content on the page, and makes them focus on the process or the dialog you showed them.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.600
So if the user is in an important process like checkout, they're checking out,

11
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.100
and it's not a good idea at all to pop up a modal dialog while they're focused on it.

12
00:00:53.100 --> 00:01:00.100
It's a process most users feel a little anxious about. They need to do it carefully, and they're focused on it.

13
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:06.100
A modal dialog would be very annoying then, so here I shouldn't use one at all.

14
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:13.100
I also won't use a modal dialog when the user has to make a decision based on other data,

15
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.100
information they still need to see, somewhere else, outside the dialog.

16
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:23.300
Then I can use a nonmodal dialog, or a page, or anything that lets them see the data they need while they decide.

